      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is considered good coding-style to use `.cast()` for casting raw pointers because `as` casts can also accidentally change the mutability of the pointer, whereas `.cast()` can only change the type and not the mutability.\n```suggestion\n            let name_buffer \u003d name.cast::\u003c[u8; ASHMEM_FULL_NAME_LEN]\u003e();\n```",
      "revId": "aff120ac970a1ec60540871e103341f5681cd393",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
