      "writtenOn": "2025-07-08T08:43:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The requirement is stronger than \"non-null\". If I called this function with `(char *) 0xdeadbeef` then that would also be incorrect even though the pointer is non-null. Generally, we just say that the pointer is valid for writing, which implies that it\u0027s non-null.",
      "range": {
